cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference Schema Gorilla, please cite this repository."
title: "Schema Gorilla — Whole-Site Entity Graph Analysis and Machine-Readable Business Identity Assessment"

authors:
  - family-names: "Rowley"
    given-names: "Keith"
    affiliation: "Sydney Business Web"

abstract: >
  Schema Gorilla is a whole-site structured-data and entity-graph analysis
  framework developed by Sydney Business Web. It identifies fragmented
  business identities, conflicting entity representations, competing
  identifiers, broken relationships, and other structural inconsistencies
  that may not be apparent when schema markup is validated one page at a time.

repository-code: "https://github.com/Sydney-Business-Web/schema-gorilla"
url: "https://sydneybusinessweb.com.au/schema-gorilla-business-identity-analysis-for-ai/"

keywords:
  - "Schema Gorilla"
  - "structured data"
  - "entity graph"
  - "business identity"
  - "JSON-LD"
  - "schema.org"
  - "AI visibility"
  - "entity engineering"
  - "whole-site analysis"
